# Per-course data & generated books are kept LOCAL, not in version control.
courses/
# ...and as a bare name too. A git worktree may reach the data through a SYMLINK named `courses`,
# and the `courses/` pattern only matches a directory -- so the symlink showed up as untracked and
# `git add -A` would have committed a machine-specific absolute path into a public repo.
courses

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Generated / large / binary artifacts (should only ever live under courses/, but belt-and-suspenders)
*.pdf
*.laz
*.npy
*.tif
*.tiff
dem_hd/
laz/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local scratch
/tmp/
*.log

# Local tooling / personal assets (kept out of the repo)
.claude/
lucaswu.golf_qr*.png

# Personal outreach drafts (letters to architects, clubs, associations). Recovered from a gitignored
# worktree where they were the only copy in existence -- git had never seen them, so pruning that
# worktree would have deleted them. Kept in the working tree so they survive; never committed, because
# they are private correspondence and this repo is public.
outreach/

# Coverage artifacts. `.coverage` is a SQLite database written by `coverage run`; it holds absolute
# paths from the machine that produced it and is meaningless anywhere else. It appeared untracked
# during a coverage audit of the test suite, which is exactly when it would have been swept into a
# commit by a careless `git add`.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Local-only legal working notes. These stay OUT of the public repo deliberately.
#
# 04 is written as a hand-to-a-challenger script ("Why each legal theory fails"). Publishing it
# names presumed adversaries, publishes our own read of our weakest points, and asserts legal
# conclusions -- including patent non-infringement, which nobody has run a freedom-to-operate search
# to support. An unsupported public assertion of non-infringement is the one line in this folder that
# could cut against us rather than for us. The FACTS that make the project defensible are in 01-03,
# which stay public; 04 only added argument.
legal/04_INDEPENDENT_CREATION_DEFENSE.md

# 08 is a dated internal audit snapshot carrying the same severity ratings ("Weak", "Frivolous") and
# an internal action checklist whose pre-release boxes read as unchecked. Its factual outcome -- the
# Esri imagery removed and rebuilt from public-domain NAIP -- is fully recorded in 07 and 01, which
# stay public. What is local is the self-assessment, not the facts.
legal/08_AUDIT_2026-07-13.md

# Audit-campaign ledger. Local working state for the /perfect campaign: what was verified, fixed,
# rejected and left open, so a re-run resumes instead of restarting. Not part of the engine and not
# a published record -- legal/ is where durable claims live. Ignored because it was written while a
# fixer held commit permission, and an untracked docs/ tree is exactly what a careless `git add -A`
# sweeps in.
docs/audit-greenbook/
